cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the thesis below. Use is non-commercial only (CC BY-NC 4.0)."
title: "Leveraging Machine Learning and Wearables Technology for Sepsis Prediction and Workflow Optimization"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility code for a BSc thesis investigating whether wearable-grade
  vital signs can predict Sepsis-3 onset on hospital general wards, using an
  etiology-specific stacked ensemble on MIMIC-IV, and assessing organizational
  implementation viability through a contextualized UTAUT framework.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Storm Petersen"
    given-names: "Nikolaj"
date-released: 2026-05-06
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
keywords:
  - sepsis prediction
  - wearable sensors
  - machine learning
  - stacked ensemble
  - MIMIC-IV
  - UTAUT
  - clinical decision support
